.TH UH7000-STREAM 1 "July 2026" "tascam-uh7000-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uh7000-stream \- explicit configuration-1 analog playback for the TASCAM UH-7000
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uh7000-stream
.RB [ \-\-seconds
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-raw
.IR FILE \||\| \-\-stdin ]
.RB [ \-\-output-only ]
.RB [ \-\-duplex-probe ]
.B \-\-execute
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uh7000-stream
temporarily selects the UH-7000 vendor USB configuration 1 and sends a stereo
48 kHz S24_3LE stream to its verified analog playback endpoint. On normal exit,
SIGINT, or SIGTERM it restores USB configuration 2 so the stock
.B snd_usb_audio
capture/control topology returns.

The stream reads endpoint 0x85 feedback and varies packet frame counts to
follow the device clock rather than assuming exactly 48 frames per millisecond.

Without a source option the command generates a bounded 1250 Hz tone at
-30 dBFS. This is intended for disconnected-output diagnostics only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-raw " FILE"
Replay a finite stereo S24_3LE, 48000 Hz raw PCM file. The file length must be
a multiple of 288 bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read stereo S24_3LE, 48000 Hz raw PCM from standard input. A duration of zero
runs until standard input closes or the process receives SIGINT/SIGTERM.
.TP
.BI \-\-seconds " N"
Run for one through ten seconds. With
.B \-\-stdin
only, zero means run until interrupted. The default is two seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-output-only
Do not claim the configuration-1 capture interface. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-duplex-probe
Claim the configuration-1 capture endpoint and print loopback metrics. This is
research diagnostics only; it is not needed for playback and can observe a
transitional short packet after a device rebind.
.TP
.B \-\-execute
Perform the stream. Without this flag the command only prints its plan.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ffmpeg -i music.wav -f s24le -ac 2 -ar 48000 - | uh7000-stream --stdin --seconds 0 --execute
uh7000-stream --seconds 2 --execute
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Disconnect speakers and headphones before using the generated tone. The command
does not apply mixer, DSP, or vendor control writes. It is an explicit analog
playback path and does not make the normal UAC2 configuration-2 playback
terminal analog-routed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uh7000ctl (1)
